<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- Cabinet INDEPENDENT outcome-monitoring watchdog.

     Verifies declared OUTCOMES actually happened (not just that processes ran):
     briefing DELIVERED, officers reflected, decisions logged, no silent cron
     failure, pipes fresh. Routes failures by tier (auto-fix / Chair / drift) and
     stamps its own heartbeat for the dead-man's switch.

     StartCalendarInterval (wall-clock, every :00 and :30) — NOT StartInterval —
     because a relative StartInterval can be silently coalesced/throttled for
     hours by the macOS power manager (root cause of the 2026-06-25 pipe stall),
     and a watchdog that silently stops firing is worse than none. Calendar
     timers fire on the wall clock and don't coalesce-stall.

     Source of truth in repo; installed + loaded with:
       cp cabinet/launchd/com.cabinet.outcome-watchdog.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
       launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.cabinet.outcome-watchdog.plist

     DISABLE (reversible):
       launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.cabinet.outcome-watchdog
       rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.cabinet.outcome-watchdog.plist   # optional, full removal

     No secrets here — the wrapper reads none (the only outbound is a localhost
     Redis trigger the Chair turns into a gated send). PATH/REDIS_HOST/TZ are set
     inside the wrapper.

     KNOWN LIMIT (MacBook): launchd does not fire while the Mac is asleep; a
     missed calendar slot fires once on wake. True 24/7 cadence needs the
     always-on Mac Mini. The dead-man's switch (pipe-watchdog, also calendar-
     scheduled) covers a watchdog that stops firing for any reason. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.cabinet.outcome-watchdog</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/nate/captains-cabinet/cabinet/scripts/run-outcome-watchdog.sh</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/nate/.cabinet/logs/outcome-watchdog.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/nate/.cabinet/logs/outcome-watchdog.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
